;; The module readline (queue 289; Modules/readline.c of CPython 3.14.10, PSF License Agreement) over a line editor of
;; pyi's own in the place of GNU readline 8's (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: 289"): the module's functions
;; as readline.c defines them over GNU's history list (1-based history_get from history_base, 0-based remove and
;; replace, stifling by `set history-size`, history files of one line an entry, history_truncate_file's last lines),
;; the hooks (startup before the prompt, pre-input after it, the completer, the matches' display), the init file
;; (INPUTRC, else ~/.inputrc, else /etc/inputrc, read at import as setup_readline's rl_initialize reads it) and
;; parse_and_bind's lines: `set VAR VALUE`, `KEY: FUNCTION` and `KEY: "MACRO"` for the keys "\C-x", "\t", "\e...",
;; Control-x, TAB, RET, ESC, DEL and the functions below. Once imported, input() on a terminal (sys.stdin and sys.stdout
;; the process's, both ttys) reads its line by the editor (call_readline's PyOS_ReadlineFunctionPointer): the terminal
;; as GNU's rl_prep_terminal sets it (no ICANON, ECHO, ICRNL, INLCR, ISTRIP, INPCK; VMIN 1), the prompt on stdout, the
;; emacs keymap's common bindings, TAB bound to self-insert as setup_readline binds it until a binding to complete
;; (GNU's rl_complete: the word back to a delimiter of set_completer_delims, the completer's matches for state 0, 1,
;; ... until a non-string, an exception ending them as on_completion's PyErr_Clear; one match replaces the word, several
;; their common prefix, a second TAB that changed nothing lists them, by the display hook when set; no completer:
;; file names), the line added to the history unless set_auto_history(False) or equal to the last.

